{
  "slug": "notif-sound",
  "name": "Notif Sound",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "A Claude Code plugin that plays notification sounds when Claude finishes responding, asks a question, or needs permission — never miss when Claude needs your attention.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **9 commands** and **4 hooks**.\n\n- **Commands** (9): `add` (Add a new sound file to the notification sounds library), `gui` (Start or stop the web GUI dashboard for managing notification sounds), `list` (List all notification sounds and show current volume), `remove` (Remove a sound file from the notification sounds library), `status` (Check plugin health: verify scripts, sounds, audio player, and hooks are working), `test` (Test play a random notification sound), `uninstall` (Cleanly uninstall the notif-sound plugin: stop GUI, remove cache, remove data), `verify` (Verify notif-sound plugin setup: check script permissions, sound files, and test playback), and 1 more\n- **Hooks** (4): `Stop`, `Notification`, `PreToolUse`, `PermissionRequest`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install notif-sound@claude-community` from `juuni26/claude-notif-sound`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "hook": 4,
    "command": 9
  },
